+Real Chromium (Playwright), fake camera = a real face photo with a RED mark in the camera image's
+top-left corner (05_* images; not included in the delivered package because they show a third-party
+person's photo), fake microphone = real speech. Server = the project's
+run.py on 127.0.0.1, fresh SQLite DB, accounts from tools/create_test_users.py. Separate browser
+contexts (cookie jars) for the proctor and every student. Values copied verbatim from the runs.
+
+1. Orientation of the frame the exam page uploads (the page's own grabBlob(320,240,0.65))
+   ORIGINAL page : red block centre x=0.94 -> RIGHT  => MIRRORED   (05_uploaded_frame_BEFORE_mirrored.jpg)
+   REPAIRED page : red mark stays left            => RAW camera image (05_uploaded_frame_AFTER_raw.jpg)
+
+2. Single student, ORIGINAL code (unmodified project): student page showed
+   Stream "Live", Analysis "Server error" (POST /student/frame 500), Frames 2.
+
+3. Single student, REPAIRED code (06_browser_e2e_after.json)
+   Active before join            : 0 ("No active students")
+   Tile appeared after join      : 1.42 s (earlier run 0.95 s), Active -> 1, no reload
+   Tile frames displayed         : 4.07 per s (bounded by the dashboard's 250 ms stream poll)
+   Frame age at the proctor      : p50 28 ms, p95 53 ms
+   Zoomed student view           : 5.88 frames per s (0.0 before the Chart.js guard)
+   Uploads blocked for 8 s       : Live ... Live, Reconnecting... (from ~5 s), Live again 1.6 s after recovery (outage_labels)
+   Speech from the fake mic      : "Suspicious audio: speech (98-100 %, YAMNet)" events on the proctor card
+   Student risk widget           : now 27 % Low, exam total (cumulative) 80 % High
+   Remaining console errors      : only CDN resources (no internet in the sandbox)
+   Experiment: 50 ms zoom refresh -> 6.38 fps (vs 5.88) = no measurable benefit -> REVERTED.
+
+4. Several students + one proctor (dashboard code as shipped vs repaired)
+                       ORIGINAL dashboard JS                 REPAIRED
+   2 students          tiles 2, Active 2, tile fps 0.0 / 4.07   tiles 2, Active 2, tile fps 4.0 / 4.0
+   5 students          tiles 5, Active 5, tile fps min 0.0,     tiles 5, Active 5, tile fps 3.47-3.73
+                       median 0.0, max 3.93 (only tile 1 moved)
+   Cause: pollStreams() iterated '#student-grid [data-sid]' which also matches each card's
+   "View Report" button -> the first button threw -> loop aborted after tile 1.
+
+5. Live alert feed (one student speaking, 25 s)
+   ORIGINAL : SSE delivered 4 messages, alertCount 4, feed children 0, counters {audio:0,total:0},
+              console: "[sse] bad message TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'style') at pushAlert"
+   REPAIRED : feed children 4, counters {audio:3,total:3}, no console errors
+   (SSE itself was verified with a raw HTTP client: 'connected', 'student_joined', 'event' delivered.)
+
+6. Server crash + restart (real run.py, kill -9, same DB, same browser cookie), probe_restart.py
+   ORIGINAL : before crash  session=fc855307 cumulative=0.0  events=1   (integrity event not in cumulative)
+              after restart session=fc855307 cumulative=0.33 events=1   (jumps on resume)
+              re-join -> NEW session (refresh resets the exam)
+   REPAIRED : before crash  session=4a7b458d cumulative=0.33 events=1
+              after restart session=4a7b458d same=True cumulative=0.33 events=1
+              re-join after restart: same session, 0.33
+              proctor card: same session, cumulative 0.33, Medium, stream live
+
+7. tools/live_diag.py replay run (no webcam here: --video = real webcam GIF of a person moving,
+   --audio = real speech, looping, so "silence" is expected to fail):
+     1 neutral        SUPPRESSED      calibration not ready ... (the replayed person keeps moving)
+     2 head_left      SUPPRESSED      never valid: head/gaze not valid (calibration calibrating)
+    10 phone          MODEL MISS      YOLOv8m produced no cell-phone box in 8 frames ...
+    11 speak          DETECTED        event 'Suspicious audio: speech (100%, YAMNet)'
+    12 silence        NOT DETECTED    FALSE audio event during silence ... (file kept playing speech)
+    13 second_person  MODEL MISS      YOLO counted 1 person in every frame ...
+   => the tool computes its verdicts from the real pipeline; it does not mark success by itself.
